From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:59:05 +0200
Subject: Test a symbol's owner before its annotations in MoveStatics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`MoveStatics.transformSym` asked `hasAnnotation(ScalaStaticAnnot)` of every
denotation brought forward through it, before checking that the symbol is a
member of a module with a companion — the only symbols it can move.
`hasAnnotation` matches each annotation's class by `derivesFrom`, which needs
that class's base classes. In a run where a class's base classes are first
computed at a late phase (a suspended-units run, asked by a backend such as
Scala Native's `genNIR`), computing them brings its parent forward through the
transformers, and `MoveStatics` then matched the parent's own `@SourceFile`
annotation against `@static` — re-entering the locked computation of
`SourceFile`'s base classes: "Cyclic reference involving class SourceFile",
escaping the run and failing the compilation. The owner checks now come
first, so a class symbol is never made to look at its annotations here.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: movestatics
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/MoveStatics.scala | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/MoveStatics.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/MoveStatics.scala
index 13741c24d4155a52c41bb0d94b7580c21c474964..832ef537c6b2203429c73e817930d913f1d3e2a7 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/MoveStatics.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/MoveStatics.scala
@@ -30,7 +30,13 @@ class MoveStatics extends MiniPhase with SymTransformer {
   override def description: String = MoveStatics.description
 
   def transformSym(sym: SymDenotation)(using Context): SymDenotation =
-    if (sym.hasAnnotation(defn.ScalaStaticAnnot) && sym.owner.is(Flags.Module) && sym.owner.companionClass.exists &&
+    // Test the owner before the annotation: `hasAnnotation` matches each annotation's class by
+    // `derivesFrom`, which computes that class's base classes. When a denotation is brought
+    // forward to a late phase while the base classes of an annotation class are being computed
+    // (a `@SourceFile`-annotated parent, as every class from a TASTy-compiled library is), that
+    // would re-enter the computation and raise a cyclic reference; only a member of a module
+    // with a companion can move, so nothing else needs its annotations looked at.
+    if (sym.owner.is(Flags.Module) && sym.owner.companionClass.exists && sym.hasAnnotation(defn.ScalaStaticAnnot) &&
         (sym.is(Flags.Method) || !(sym.isMutableVarOrAccessor && sym.owner.companionClass.is(Flags.Trait)) && !sym.symbol.name.is(LazyVarHandleName))) {
       sym.owner.asClass.delete(sym.symbol)
       sym.owner.companionClass.asClass.enter(sym.symbol)
